{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Destination"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each destination its batches in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order the events were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns. Batches that arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its oldest batch when full, so a destination that falls behind doesn’t hold up the others."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The delivery reports each batch dropped. Once the destination has caught up, it gets the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped batch’s records that a store keeps, read back from the store, after the newer batches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it received meanwhile; those kept in memory only are lost."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" should return as soon as the batch is somewhere it won’t be lost, and honour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation: a delivery waits for it before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled. Until it returns, this destination’s later batches wait in its buffer. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination handles its own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is what tells the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose "},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is set may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have reached it in an earlier run."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\